  "summary": "When Tim Costello was in year 9 (about 14 or 15 years old), he asked his teacher if being poor was something that just happens naturally, like the tide or the sunrise. Now, he believes that poverty isn’t natural; it happens because of the decisions made by people in power (policy). Costello is now 69 years old and has spent more than 30 years working to fight poverty in Australia. He has traveled to dangerous and disaster-affected places, was once mayor of St Kilda, has written books, and is known as an important figure in Australia. Some people confuse him with his brother Peter Costello, who was a government treasurer. When the writer went to see Tim Costello, people wanted to know if it was the politician brother or the religious one. Tim is famous for being a Baptist minister and for leading World Vision, a large charity, for 13 years."
}
